;; Clojure's eval level's divergences from its reference (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3,
;; RPS16): the classes every non-pass of the level's checks falls into, in the format of
;; test/goi/divergences.edn. A case's class is the first whose :match finds its "RESULT REASON":
;; - Clojure's suite (test/arbace-go-results.edn against upstream's, test/baseline-results.edn: every
;;   assertion passes upstream), one case per test or namespace that does not pass or does not run:
;;   "skip NS: why" (a namespace not run), "skip NS/TEST: why" (a test not run), "fail NS/TEST (fail
;;   F, error E)", "error NS/TEST (fail 0, error E)"; test.generative's "fail spec S", "error load NS";
;; - the oracle (test/oracle/known-go-amd64-frozen.edn, the eval level's files): "known REASON", the
;;   known mismatch's reason.
;; :kind :design (by design, decided) or :deferred (to be built, named where); :decided where the
;; decision is recorded, :pending when it is recorded nowhere (the user's to decide). bin/reap
;; judges it (test/reap/main.ae); bin/clojure-tests --divergences judges a run of the suite.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 ;; the suite: namespaces and tests that do not run
 {:id :gen-class
  :title "gen-class: a superclass the Go build's Java forms cannot extend (ClassLoader)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gen-class defines its class at run time as a Java form (CDR3's first stage, arbace/genclass.ae), so genclass.examples loads and 6 of genclass's 8 tests pass; protected-final-access's ProtectedFinalTester extends java.lang.ClassLoader, which is not among the classes the Java forms may extend (arbace.j2g.model/class-supers): its stand-in's constructor throws. CDR3's second stage: ClassLoader a class-super with its protected constructors and final methods (a j2g and jrt change, a build)"
  :decided "CDR3 (the user, 2026-11-05): gen-class in two stages, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^error clojure\.test-clojure\.genclass/protected-final-access "]}
 {:id :xml
  :title "XML: SAX (arbace.xml)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "arbace.xml loads but parses nothing: SAX (java.xml's xerces closure) is not in the shipped world, so clojure-xml's one test errs at SAXParserFactory"
  :decided "built when the night's measurement of the closure is under 10 MB (doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md, \"As built\"); doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; CDR5 (the user, 2026-11-05): SAX and StAX in the shipped world if the growth is under 10 MB, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.clojure-xml: "]}
 {:id :serialization
  :title "Java serialization (ObjectOutputStream)"
  :kind :design
  :why "java.io.ObjectOutputStream and ObjectInputStream are not in the Go build: serialization's namespace, and java-interop's test-proxy-non-serializable (which also needs arbace.inspector's Swing list-model); the oracle's one case (the proxy itself works)"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; doc/go/J2G-SPEC.md §12; CDR6 (the user, 2026-11-05): a 2-day spike, then the user's decision, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.serialization: "
          #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-non-serializable: "
          #"^known Out of the Go build for good \(B1-PLAN's D6"]}
 {:id :desktop
  :title "java.desktop: java.awt.Point and Color"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "java-interop's test-dot (java.awt.Point) and test-bean (java.awt.Color): java.desktop is not in the Go build"
  :decided "built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\"), closed by the night's conversion and build; doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; CDR4 (b) (the user, 2026-11-05): Point, Point2D and an sRGB Color in the shipped world, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/(test-bean|test-dot): "]}
 {:id :tools-deps
  :title "tools.deps' jars (arbace.repl.deps)"
  :kind :design
  :why "arbace.repl.deps adds libraries' jars to the class path at run time (tools.deps); the Go build loads no jars"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; CDR9 (the user, 2026-11-05)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.repl\.deps: "]}
 {:id :javadoc-url
  :title "java.javadoc's javadoc-url-test: java.sql.Connection is not in the Go build"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "javadoc-url-test's java.sql.Connection assertion errs at Class/forName: java.sql is not in the Go build's world (D6). Its other two errors (Class.getModule) are fixed: jrt's java.lang.Module (RPS55 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"As built: RPS55\"; doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\")"
  :decided "CDR4 (b) (the user, 2026-11-05): java.sql in the shipped world, built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\"), closed by the night's conversion and build; doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; RPS55 (a): the java.sql assertion by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS40-RPS59\")"
  :match [#"^error clojure\.test-clojure\.java\.javadoc/javadoc-url-test \(fail 0, error 1\)"]}
 {:id :class-files
  :title "class files: the Go build writes and reads none"
  :kind :design
  :why "compile writes no class files and ASM is gone (clj-1208 loads a deftype AOT-compiled from compilation.load-ns; test-proxy-method-order reads the proxy's class file with ASM, genclass's gen-interface-source-file the interface's)"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-SURVEY.md D13; doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 23"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/clj-1208: " #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-method-order: "
          #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.genclass/gen-interface-source-file: "]}
 {:id :xml-stream
  :title "javax.xml.stream (reflect's invoke-checks-accessibility)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test reflects over javax.xml.stream's classes, which are not in the Go build's world (java.xml stays out of the shipped world, D6; the SAX cut, RPS56)"
  :decided "CDR5 (the user, 2026-11-05): SAX and StAX in the shipped world if the growth is under 10 MB, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md; RPS134 (b), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, Decided (2026-10-28)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.reflect/invoke-checks-accessibility: "]}
 ;; the suite: tests that fail
 {:id :q1-typing
  :title "the evaluator's typing of a primitive fn's call (CDR2)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "primitive-return-decl and incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws are compile-time checks that need a ^long call's primitive type, not a primitive interface: no recur-mismatch warning, no \"Cannot coerce long to int\" while the evaluator typed the call Object. Built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 32: InvokeExpr.parse's RT/longCast, MethodExpr.checkTypedArgs), a runtime change closed by the night's build"
  :decided "CDR2 (a) (the user, 2026-11-05), doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md; Q1 (a) kept"
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/(primitive-return-decl|incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws) "]}
 {:id :q1-boxed-prims
  :title "the evaluator's fns are boxed (Q1): no primitive interfaces"
  :kind :design
  :why "a fn made at run time is one Go type calling invoke, not invokePrim: it implements none of IFn's primitive interfaces (IFn$LL, IFn$LOL ...), so a ^long fn of the REPL is no IFn$LL (the oracle's native.ae cases, which call .invokePrim or test instance? IFn$LL; the suite's typing cases are :q1-typing since CDR2)"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^known By design \(doc/go/EVAL-PLAN\.md, Q1"]}
 ;; the oracle's known mismatches (eval)
 {:id :locales
  :title "locale data: root and English only"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the shipped build's locale data are java.base's root and English alone (JRT_LOCALES defaults to none); another language takes the root's data, where the JVM has jdk.localedata's"
  :decided "CDR1 (the user, 2026-11-05): measured under JRT_LOCALES=common at night, then the shipped default common (+8.9 MB) if they pass, reversing the decision of 2026-10-11; the user, 2026-10-11; doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Text and locales\", TM4, TL5"
  :match [#"^known The shipped build's locale data are java\.base's root and English alone"]}
 {:id :security-providers
  :title "security providers: SUN, SunRsaSign, SunEC and SunJCE only"
  :kind :design
  :why "java.security's other eight providers are not in the Go build and fail to load, as a provider the JDK cannot find (ten before the JCA, doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, F1, added SunRsaSign and SunEC)"
  :decided "doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Security\", SC4"
  :match [#"^known The providers of the Go build are SUN(, SunRsaSign, SunEC)? and SunJCE"]}
 {:id :security-manager
  :title "java.lang.SecurityManager not in the world"
  :kind :design
  :why "JEP 486: the Security Manager is permanently disabled and nothing of the program names the class, so (resolve 'java.lang.SecurityManager) is nil; RT's default imports dropped it"
  :decided "doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 11"
  :match [#"^known java\.lang\.SecurityManager is not in the Go build's world"]}
 {:id :identity-hash
  :title "identity hashes (not reproducible)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the JVM recorded HotSpot's identity hash of a StringBuilder, a per-thread xorshift sequence"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, phase 2B (as decided for #object printing)"
  :match [#"^known Not reproducible, as decided for #object printing"]}
 {:id :main-since-v4
  :title "main's divergences from the frozen reference (v4)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the oracle's reference is arbace-for-java-26-v4's jar; main names two ambiguous MultiFn classes in the order of their names (ac8b9718), and its loaders look for .ae first (the .ae rename), so its not-found message names .ae"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-NOTES.md, \"S4: the oracle's reference\"; commit ac8b9718; the .ae rename (2026-10-11)"
  :match [#"^known Divergences of main from the frozen reference"]}
 {:id :method-invoke-message
  :title "a message's wording: Method.invoke on a receiver of another class"
  :kind :design
  :why "jrt's Method.invoke words it as JDK 26's DirectMethodHandleAccessor does ('object of type java.lang.Long is not an instance of java.lang.String'), the JVM Arbace's call 'object is not an instance of java.lang.String'; the exception's class is the same. Recorded as a known mismatch only: by design or to align the message is the user's (RPS19)"
  :decided "RPS19 (a), by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^known Message: a qualified method value \(String/\.indexOf\)"]}
]
